Janis Papanagnou <janis_papanagnou@hotmail.com> wrote:
> On 29/07/10 00:14, Thomas Pornin wrote:
>> 
>> Without polymorph control, you can still get predictable polymorphs
>> in some situations:
>> [...]
>> - if you wear dragon scales or dragon scale mail, then you turn into
>> the corresponding dragon -- and the scales/scale mail are not lost in
>> the process (you get them back when you turn back to human form);
>
> Mind, as I reported recently, that this is not true if you polymorph a
> second time (while being a dragon); the scales are lost in that case.
> (Sadly I've learned that the hard way.)

That statement is a bit too drastic.

While being polymorphed into a dragon and getting polymorphed again,
the usual polymorph rules for armor apply:

If you are small, the DSM falls to the ground and if you are too
large, you destroy the DSM by breaking out of it.

So you don't lose your DSM for sure when being polymorphed as a
dragon.


BTW when wearing a DSM and a ring of polymorph control and after being
asked what form you want to polymorph into answering with something
else than the dragon color of your DSM, you might lose the DSM, too.

